---An item product definition.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html)
---@class (exact) ItemProductPrototype:ProductPrototypeBase
---@
---
---Whether quality roll affects quality of products given. If set to `false`, result of a quality roll will be ignored and an item of quality based on quality of selected recipe will be given.
---
---Note: This may not work as expected outside of recipes (e.g. in mining drills).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23affected_by_quality#affected_by_quality)
---@field affected_by_quality? boolean
---@
---
---When set to true, the item produced will be produced fresh (using percent\_spoiled) even when ingredients were spoiled.
---
---Note: This may not work as expected outside of recipes (e.g. in mining drills).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23always_fresh#always_fresh)
---@field always_fresh? boolean
---@
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23amount#amount)
---@field amount? uint16
---@
---
---Only loaded, and mandatory if `amount` is not defined.
---
---If set to a number that is less than `amount_min`, the game will use `amount_min` instead.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23amount_max#amount_max)
---@field amount_max? uint16
---@
---
---Only loaded, and mandatory if `amount` is not defined.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23amount_min#amount_min)
---@field amount_min? uint16
---@
---
---Probability that a craft will yield one additional product. Also applies to bonus crafts caused by productivity.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23extra_count_fraction#extra_count_fraction)
---@field extra_count_fraction? float
---@
---
---Amount that should be deducted from any productivity induced bonus crafts.
---
---This value can safely be set larger than the maximum expected craft amount, any excess is ignored.
---
---This value is ignored when [allow\_productivity](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/RecipePrototype.html%23allow_productivity#allow_productivity) is `false`.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23ignored_by_productivity#ignored_by_productivity)
---@field ignored_by_productivity? uint16
---@
---
---Amount that should not be included in the item production statistics, typically with a matching ingredient having the same amount set as [ignored\_by\_stats](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemIngredientPrototype.html%23ignored_by_stats#ignored_by_stats).
---
---If `ignored_by_stats` is larger than the amount crafted (for instance due to probability) it will instead show as consumed.
---
---Products with `ignored_by_stats` defined will not be set as recipe through the circuit network when using the product's item-signal.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23ignored_by_stats#ignored_by_stats)
---@field ignored_by_stats? uint16
---@
---
---The name of an [ItemPrototype](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23name#name)
---@field name ItemID
---@
---
---Must be >= `0` and < `1`.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23percent_spoiled#percent_spoiled)
---@field percent_spoiled? float
---@
---
---Amount of quality levels up or down this product will be adjusted.
---
---This is the difference between the quality of the recipe and the quality of the product. For a vanilla example, when epic is selected for recipe quality, a product with quality change `1` would be legendary quality, not epic.
---
---Note: This may not work as expected outside of recipes (e.g. in mining drills).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23quality_change#quality_change)
---@field quality_change? int8
---@
---
---Highest possible quality of item that will be given. If not provided but `quality_min` is given, it will be set to the highest quality from a quality chain to which `quality_min` belongs. Must belong to the same quality chain as `quality_min` and be equal or better, meaning later in the chain when following [QualityPrototype::next](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/QualityPrototype.html%23next#next).
---
---Note: If this is used outside of recipes (e.g. by mining drills), setting this to a custom quality chain will discard the quality roll.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23quality_max#quality_max)
---@field quality_max? QualityID
---@
---
---Lowest possible quality of item that will be given. If not provided but `quality_max` is given, it will be set to the lowest quality from a quality chain to which `quality_max` belongs. When set, if the recipe would produce items from a different quality chain (due to quality of the recipe or quality roll), `quality_min` will be used for the quality instead.
---
---Note: If this is used outside of recipes (e.g. by mining drills), setting this to a custom quality chain will discard the quality roll.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23quality_min#quality_min)
---@field quality_min? QualityID
---@
---
---When set to true, if the recipe successfully finishes crafting without spoiling, the result is produced fresh (non-spoiled).
---
---Note: This may not work as expected outside of recipes (e.g. in mining drills).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23reset_freshness_on_craft#reset_freshness_on_craft)
---@field reset_freshness_on_craft? boolean
---@
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemProductPrototype.html%23type#type)
---@field type "item"
---@
